From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: appxdeploymentclient: deploy, register and remove packages

PackageManager's AddPackageAsync, RegisterPackageAsync and
RemovePackageAsync were stubs, so no MSIX or AppX package could be
installed: Store apps, winget's MSIX packages, Add-AppxPackage.

- AddPackageAsync (and UpdatePackageAsync) of a file: URI: the package's
  signature must be trusted (WinVerifyTrust through the AppX SIP, patch
  0037) -- unsigned, untrusted and tampered packages are refused with that
  HRESULT as the DeploymentResult's ExtendedErrorCode. It is read with
  appxpackaging (every file checked against the signed block map), extracted
  to %ProgramFiles%\WindowsApps\<full name> -- or, for a user who may not
  write there, %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\WindowsApps\<full name> -- with its
  AppxManifest.xml, block map and signature beside it, and registered for
  the user. File names are checked: nothing absolute, nothing with "..".
- RegisterPackageAsync of a loose AppxManifest.xml in development mode
  (developer mode on: AppModelUnlock\AllowDevelopmentWithoutDevLicense)
  registers the folder it is in.
- A registration is HKCU\Software\Wine\AppModel\Packages\<full name>:
  identity, InstallLocation, display properties, and the Start menu
  shortcuts made for its applications (one per Application with an app
  list entry), which RemovePackageAsync deletes with the registration and,
  unless it was a development registration, the files.
- FindPackages* return the user's packages as Package objects: IPackage
  (Id, InstalledLocation -- a StorageFolder that knows its path --,
  IsFramework), IPackage2 (display properties), IPackage3
  (GetAppListEntriesAsync; an AppListEntry's LaunchAsync starts the
  application in its folder), IPackageId.
- The operations are IAsyncOperationWithProgress<DeploymentResult,
  DeploymentProgress> running on the thread pool; a failure ends in Error
  with the DeploymentResult's ErrorText and ExtendedErrorCode set.
- Not yet: bundles (.msixbundle, .appxbundle), dependency packages, app
  execution aliases, deployment for another user, cancellation.

windows.applicationmodel:model now registers, finds, launches and removes
its test package (174 tests, and 44 in the packaged application, 0
failures); the test no longer assumes that a system has packages already
(a Windows one always does, a fresh prefix never), and the todo_wine it had
for the queries is gone. Gate: make test-appx (test/deploy-probe.c).

